WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.660
Good morning Hank! It's Tuesday. 
Well this is a nice turn of events! They're decorated!

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:08.680
Hank, I haven't been getting a lot of sleep lately. And as you can probably tell puff levels are a little bit high.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.080
But I don't want to talk about that today, I want to talk about my favorite subreddits!

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.420
For those who are unaware Reddit is a link aggregation site with lots of different communities called "Subreddits".

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:22.900
And while I often find browsing an uncurated reddit to be a little bit unpleasant. And at times even kind of toxic.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:27.980
There are also many wonderful corners of Reddit including for the record reddit.com/r/nerdfighters

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.520
Where you can follow along with all the happenings in Nerdfighteria.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.400
Okay, first we have "Children Falling Over" which is just a collection of mostly

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:41.220
wholesome GIFs of children falling over. I mean who among us does not want to watch this kid fall off a diving board.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.240
Over and over and over again?

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:47.580
And speaking of over and over and over another of my favorite subreddits is "Better Every Loop"

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.540
Which is a collection of GIFs that get better with every loop.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:55.080
An example being this GIF entitled "Four Girls One Rat" in which a group of young people

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:58.960
devise a brilliant and complicated strategy for ridding their home of a rat.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.180
Wait, wait for it! Wait for it. YES!!!!

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:04.920
Oh I could watch that again and again but alas we can't 'cuz we have to move on.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.640
OOOHNOWAIT! I just realized I've already said "JIF"several times in this video

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:13.280
So everyone's gonna be mad at me for my pronunciation and flame wars are going to erupt in the comments.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.780
Even though for the record both pronunciations are entirely correct.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:19.740
In fact I'm just going to use both pronunciations to make sure that I infuriate everyone.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.220
Right, Okay. Let's move on to "Birds With Arms",

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:27.680
which sounds like some kind of weapons related euphemism but in fact is  a subreddit devoted to ...birds with arms.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:31.820
They got like owls with arms. roosters with arms, hawks with arms.

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:34.900
Basically all of the major birds but with arms.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.900
Somewhat more sophisticated is the subreddit "Internet is Beautiful",

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.020
which introduces you to beautiful websites all around the world.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:44.860
From one that allows you to listen to live radio anywhere on the planet

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:47.880
to a website where google AI tries to guess what your doodles are.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:52.460
Basically it's like playing Pictionary against google and it turns out that google is very good at Pictionary!

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:56.520
That AI still cant figure out which videos to demonetize but it's great at Pictionary (Sarcastic tone).

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:02.620
Also in the "is Beautiful" category "Data is Beautiful". A subreddit that shares interesting and beautifully presented data.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:07.120
Like this web tool exploring which countries are emitting the most carbon and from what source.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.300
Then we have "Rupauls Drag Race" which is full of screenshots and fan art.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.960
And GIFs about the best reality TV show currently on the air.

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:17.320
Another of my pop culture favorites is the subreddit "Empire Did Nothing Wrong."

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:22.540
Which is devoted to the fan theory that in the Star Wars universe the Empire is actually good.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:24.300
And the Rebel Alliance are the bad guys.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:28.340
Okay let's move on to "Nature is F*ing Lit" But with the actual curse word.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:31.580
This subreddit explores all the way that nature is- you know- F*ing Lit.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:34.600
Like this crab using two sea anemones to protect himself.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.980
There are also great collaborative communities on Reddit.

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:41.920
Like "Reddit Gets Drawn". Where people submit photographs and then other people draw them.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.600
So that this dog for instance becomes This!

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.540
And this! and this!

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:51.580
That just makes me happy! As does "Oddly Satisfying" a community devoted to images and animations

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:54.280
That are oddly satisfying. Like this one is called "Double Domino"

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:57.880
And at first you're like "yeah IDK that's reasonably satisfying..."

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:01.560
But then if you just wait for a second-

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:05.080
Oh! Now that! THAT is oddly satisfying!

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:09.280
I also love the subreddit "Imaginary Maps". As readers of Paper Towns will be unsurprised to learn.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:13.940
It does contain the occasional copywrite trap map. But it's mostly somewhat fantastical maps.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:17.320
Like majority language spoken at home in the Republic of Skyrim.

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:18.560
Or REALLY fantastical maps.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.700
Like New York State High Speed Rail 2030.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.980
And lastly there is a very weird subreddit called "High Quality GIFs."

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:32.780
In which people devote many many hours to creating astonishingly, stupidly, high quality GIFs.

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:36.000
And even more weirdly almost all of them are so called "Meta."

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.940
Which is to say that they are mostly JIFs about GIFing. Or possibly GIFs about JIFing.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:47.700
"High Quality Gifs is one of those places where the longer you hang around the better it gets and that's my favorite kind of internet community.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.140
In fact it's the kind I hope we have here.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:54.660
Okay Hank! I have to get back to work but at some point I will need a break. So I hope you let me know in comments what your favorite

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:57.240
corners of the internet are on Reddit or elsewhere.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:59.760
HANK! DFTBA. I will see you on Friday.

